schema GlueAwsmUpboundIoV1beta1DataCatalogEncryptionSettingsStatusAtProviderDataCatalogEncryptionSettingsConnectionPasswordEncryption:
    r"""
    When connection password protection is enabled, the Data Catalog uses a customer-provided key to encrypt the password as part of CreateConnection or UpdateConnection and store it in the ENCRYPTED_PASSWORD field in the connection properties. You can enable catalog encryption or only password encryption. see Connection Password Encryption.

    Attributes
    ----------
    awsKmsKeyId : str, default is Undefined, optional
        A KMS key ARN that is used to encrypt the connection password. If connection password protection is enabled, the caller of CreateConnection and UpdateConnection needs at least kms:Encrypt permission on the specified AWS KMS key, to encrypt passwords before storing them in the Data Catalog.
    returnConnectionPasswordEncrypted : bool, default is Undefined, optional
        When set to true, passwords remain encrypted in the responses of GetConnection and GetConnections. This encryption takes effect independently of the catalog encryption.
    """


    awsKmsKeyId?: str

    returnConnectionPasswordEncrypted?: bool


schema GlueAwsmUpboundIoV1beta1DataCatalogEncryptionSettingsStatusAtProviderDataCatalogEncryptionSettingsEncryptionAtRest:
    r"""
    Specifies the encryption-at-rest configuration for the Data Catalog. see Encryption At Rest.

    Attributes
    ----------
    catalogEncryptionMode : str, default is Undefined, optional
        The encryption-at-rest mode for encrypting Data Catalog data. Valid values: DISABLED, SSE-KMS, SSE-KMS-WITH-SERVICE-ROLE.
    catalogEncryptionServiceRole : str, default is Undefined, optional
        The ARN of the AWS IAM role used for accessing encrypted Data Catalog data.
    sseAwsKmsKeyId : str, default is Undefined, optional
        The ARN of the AWS KMS key to use for encryption at rest.
    """


    catalogEncryptionMode?: str

    catalogEncryptionServiceRole?: str

    sseAwsKmsKeyId?: str


